Go 1.27 changes gzip-compressed output, affecting the compressed
layer digests and sizes produced by go-containerregistry.

Several tests rely on hardcoded SHA256 digests and compressed sizes
generated by older Go versions. These expectations cause test
failures with Go 1.27 even though the underlying uncompressed data
and image functionality remain unchanged.

Replace compression-dependent expectations with dynamically
calculated values and consistency checks where appropriate.

Preserve coverage for layer contents, digest and size reporting,
image manifests, stream processing, and registry upload progress.

This allows the tests to run across Go versions without depending
on the exact output of a particular gzip implementation.
